  "report_cuvette_002": {
    "id": "report_cuvette_002",
    "document": "UV-Vis Spectrophotometric Quantification of Aqueous Copper(II) Ions. Abstract: The optical absorbance of aqueous copper(II) sulfate was evaluated across the range 0.010 M to 0.100 M at lambda_max = 635 nm. The system obeyed the Beer-Lambert law with linear correlation R^2 = 0.9997 and calculated molar absorptivity epsilon = 12.04 L/(mol\u00b7cm). Methodology: Serial dilutions prepared in 50 mL volumetric flasks. Standard 1.00 cm path length quartz cuvette loaded. Spectrophotometer zeroed against blank DI water at 635 nm. Conclusion: The molar absorptivity was determined with high precision. The system serves as an exemplary calibration standard for unknown concentration assays.",
    "metadata": {
      "title": "UV-Vis Spectrophotometric Quantification of Aqueous Copper(II) Ions",
      "experiment_type": "Analytical Spectroscopy",
      "author": "Marcus Vance, Optical Metrology Lab",
      "source_file": "report_cuvette_absorbance_study.json"
    },
